          "returnType": "void",
          "description": "Stop the step and every branch it started, now. Their finally blocks run synchronously, innermost first, while this call is still on the stack, and owned operations are cancelled; a step that cancels itself is closed when it reaches its next yield. A step that already ended is unaffected. Cancellation is cooperative: it closes the step's generator at the yield where it waits. A finally block that waits again is not resumed, and work the step handed to code outside the sequencer, such as a promise, keeps running; pass SequenceContext.signal to APIs that accept an AbortSignal to stop it."
        }
      ],
